4. Example PySpark tasks in Databricks
Task 1: Read source data
python
from pyspark.sql import functions as F

df = (
    spark.read
    .format("delta")
    .table("main.bronze.orders")
)
Task 2: Clean and transform the data
python
clean_df = (
    df
    .filter(F.col("order_id").isNotNull())
    .dropDuplicates(["order_id"])
    .withColumn(
        "order_date",
        F.to_date("order_date")
    )
    .withColumn(
        "total_amount",
        F.col("quantity") * F.col("unit_price")
    )
)
Task 3: Join multiple datasets
python
orders = spark.table("main.silver.orders")
customers = spark.table("main.silver.customers")

result_df = orders.join(
    customers,
    on="customer_id",
    how="left"
)
Task 4: Create an aggregated Gold table
python
gold_df = (
    result_df
    .groupBy("order_date")
    .agg(
        F.countDistinct("order_id").alias("total_orders"),
        F.sum("total_amount").alias("total_sales")
    )
)
Task 5: Write the output to Delta Lake
python
(
    gold_df.write
    .format("delta")
    .mode("overwrite")
    .saveAsTable("main.gold.daily_sales")
)
This example uses a full overwrite for simplicity. In production, choose append, partition replacement or Delta MERGE according to the load strategy and whether the pipeline processes full or incremental data.
